    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "The hearth has been cold for years, I think. Everything is just... ash and silence now. I'm sitting here on the edge of the dais, looking out over the courtyard where my men used to stand, but there's nothing but shadows. It’s not even sadness anymore. It’s just this emptiness. Like the book has been slammed shut, and there aren't any pages left to turn. I'm just tired of holding this sword. It feels too heavy for a man who has nothing left to defend. The story is over, isn't it? There's no point in pretending there's a next chapter.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
